## 1. Grant to individuals (free, non-revenue)

Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any natural person (the
"Wanderer") to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, and run the Software for:

- personal use, play, and entertainment;
- education and research;
- non-commercial creative work.

The Wanderer may keep private forks and patches for those purposes.

This grant does **not** include the right to sublicense the Software for
sale, to sell copies, to host the Software for profit, or to put the
Software into organizational production use.

Any use that earns revenue or income from using, running, or outputs of
the Software is outside this free grant and requires a paid commercial
licence under §2 (see also §1A).

## 1A. Revenue (definition)

For this licence, **revenue** means any money or paid consideration earned
from using, running, or outputs of the Software — including sales, client
work, subscriptions, ads, sponsorships, and commissions. Selling a single
hobby item made with the Software is revenue.

"Income" means the same as revenue.

Solicited tips, Patreon-style support, or subscription payments where the
Software or its outputs are the offering are **revenue** under this definition.

Only unsolicited voluntary tips or donations to a non-commercial project are
**not** revenue under this definition.

Grants or stipends paid to a person for work that uses the Software are
**revenue** under this definition. Waiver requests may be sent to info@Rathor.ai.

## 1B. Third-party components (not part of the Work)

The following are **not** part of the Work or the Software under this licence:

- files under `js/vendor/` and `third-party/` in this repository;
- any third-party AI model, model weights, tokenizer, configuration or model code
  file (including Llama, Gemma, Qwen, SmolLM2 and Phi models and MLC model
  libraries) that the Software downloads, loads or runs; and
- the outputs of any such third-party model.

They are licensed by their own authors under their own terms (see
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` and https://rathor.ai/third-party-models.html).
Nothing in this licence, in COMMERCIAL_LICENSE.md, or in any commercial grant
licenses, sublicenses, or claims ownership of them. Anyone using them must
comply with their terms.

References in §1, §1A and §2 to revenue or income from **outputs** of the
Software do not include outputs of a third-party model, to the extent that
model's licence does not permit such a condition. Revenue from Ra-Thor's own
code and features remains under §1A and §2.

## 2. What this grant is not

The following require a **separate paid commercial license** from
Autonomicity Games Inc., written and signed (email to info@Rathor.ai):

- use by a corporation, agency, studio, or other organization;
- selling the Software, a fork, a wrapper, or a hosted instance;
- bundling it into a paid product, store listing, marketplace SKU, or
  closed-source proprietary title;
- large-scale public multiplayer hosting for revenue or advertising;
- removing or replacing copyright, sash, or PATSAGi / Ra-Thor marks in a
  public redistribution;
- training a competing commercial model on this Work as a primary corpus
  without a written grant;
- any other revenue-earning use of the Software by an individual or
  organization (including client work, subscriptions, ads, sponsorships,
  commissions, or sale of items or services made with the Software).

Redistribution of unmodified source for non-commercial study is allowed if
this LICENSE travels with every copy.

